Description: run Windows PE in QEMU/KVM from a Linux terminal
 winpe_terminal starts a Windows PE virtual machine with QEMU/KVM and passes
 the Windows command prompt through to the Linux terminal using the native
 Emergency Management Services console.
 .
 It is meant for dual-boot users who need Windows-native maintenance tools
 such as chkdsk on their own partitions without rebooting. Only partitions the
 user explicitly whitelists and connects are exposed, through a synthetic MBR
 disk served over a private NBD channel.
 .
 Windows PE itself is not part of this package. The first run of
 "sudo winpe_terminal prepare" fetches the official Microsoft components after
 asking you to read and accept Microsoft's licence, then builds the image
 locally.
